<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="csrf-token" content={get_csrf_token()} />
    <meta name="llms" content="/llms.txt" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=EB+Garamond:ital@0;1&family=Inconsolata:wght@500&family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <.live_title default="" suffix="  - Jamie Curle">
      {assigns[:page_title]}
    </.live_title>
    <Layouts.meta_tags
      page_title={assigns[:page_title]}
      page_description={assigns[:page_description]}
      og_image={assigns[:og_image]}
      og_type={assigns[:og_type] || "website"}
      url={Phoenix.Controller.current_url(@conn)}
    />
    <%!-- standard.site: ties this page to its document record on Bluesky --%>
    <link
      :if={assigns[:standard_document_uri]}
      rel="site.standard.document"
      href={assigns[:standard_document_uri]}
    />
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" title="Jamie Curle" href={~p"/feed.xml"} />
    <link
      :if={JamieWeb.MarkdownRenderer.has_markdown?(@conn.path_info)}
      rel="alternate"
      type="text/markdown"
      href={@conn.request_path}
      title="LLM-readable version"
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href={~p"/favicon.ico"} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href={~p"/favicon-32x32.png"} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href={~p"/favicon-16x16.png"} />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href={~p"/apple-touch-icon.png"} />
    <link rel="manifest" href={~p"/site.webmanifest"} />
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/css/app.css"} />
    <script defer phx-track-static type="text/javascript" src={~p"/assets/js/app.js"}>
    </script>
    <script>
      (() => {
        const setTheme = (theme) => {
          if (theme === "system") {
            localStorage.removeItem("phx:theme");
            document.documentElement.removeAttribute("data-theme");
          } else {
            localStorage.setItem("phx:theme", theme);
            document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
          }
        };
        if (!document.documentElement.hasAttribute("data-theme")) {
          setTheme(localStorage.getItem("phx:theme") || "system");
        }
        window.addEventListener("storage", (e) => e.key === "phx:theme" && setTheme(e.newValue || "system"));

        window.addEventListener("phx:set-theme", (e) => setTheme(e.target.dataset.phxTheme));
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <Layouts.body_tag body_id={assigns[:body_id]} body_classes={assigns[:body_classes] || []}>
    <header>
      <div class="header-content">
        <a href={~p"/"} class="wordmark" id="wordmark">Jamie Curle</a>
        <nav class="primary-nav">
          <a href={~p"/"} data-nav="home">Home</a>
          <a href={~p"/posts"} data-nav="blog">Blog</a>
          <a href={~p"/about"} data-nav="about">About</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>
    <main>
      {@inner_content}
    </main>
    <%!-- the footer is a dark poster: the bio as a statement, three link
         columns on hairlines, the colophon, and the name set full width --%>
    <footer>
      <div class="footer-content">
        <div class="bio">
          <p>
            Jamie Curle is a well rounded human being living and
            operating in Northumberland, UK. He spends his time between
            technology, his workshop and restoring ancient woodland. He is
            waiting for AI's killer feature  &mdash; finishing DIY projects.
          </p>
        </div>

        <nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Elsewhere">
          <section>
            <h2>Treeworld</h2>
            <ol>
              <li>
                <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@lifeoftreedom/videos"><span>YouTube</span></a>
              </li>
              <li><a href="https://lifeoftreedom.com/"><span>Life Of Treedom</span></a></li>
            </ol>
          </section>
          <section>
            <h2>Techworld</h2>
            <ol>
              <li><a href="https://jamiecurle.ltd"><span>My Company</span></a></li>
              <li>
                <a href="https://heem.team"><span>My product forge / idea factory</span></a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="https://exercism.org/profiles/jamiecurle"><span>Exercism</span></a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/jamiecurle" title="Jamie Curle on Github">
                  <span>Github</span>
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jamie-curle/" title="Jamie Curle LinkedIn">
                  <span>LinkedIn</span>
                </a>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>
          <section>
            <h2>Navigation</h2>
            <ol>
              <li><a href={~p"/about"}><span>About</span></a></li>
              <li><a href="/"><span>Blog</span></a></li>
              <li><a href="https://bsky.app/profile/curle.io"><span>Contact</span></a></li>
              <li><a href={~p"/feed.xml"} title="Atom Feed"><span>Feed</span></a></li>
              <li><a href={~p"/privacy"}><span>Privacy</span></a></li>
            </ol>
          </section>
        </nav>

        <div class="colophon">
          <p>
            A (<i>mostly</i>) handrolled site designed and engineered by me in Elixir, making extensive use of Phoenix,
            LiveView, Ecto and mdex. Built into a Docker image, ran in a Docker Compose file and
            deployed out to a Docker swarm running on a Raspberry Pi in a cupboard somewhere in my house, served through
            a Cloudflare tunnel. Yes, I can do the things. <a href="https://github.com/jamiecurle/dotcom">Source on GitHub</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Design &amp; content &copy; Jamie Curle 2026 all rights reserved. No reuse or reproduction
            of content permitted for any non-personal use, including for
            <a href="/llms.txt"> AI training purposes</a>
            except where allowed in <a href="/robots.txt">robots.txt</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="wordmark" aria-hidden="true">Jamie Curle</p>
    </footer>
  </Layouts.body_tag>
</html>
